From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:21:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(modal): run the deploying Studio's trainer code on
 Modal

The Modal app runs ghcr.io/open-edge-platform/physicalai-trainer-cuda:main,
whose trainer and training packages come from upstream main, not from
this checkout. A Studio feature that needs trainer-side code (early
stopping) could therefore never run on Modal, however often it was
redeployed.

modal_app.py now mounts this checkout's src/trainer and src/training
(without __pycache__) at /opt/physicalai-studio/src, and train() puts
that path first on sys.path before importing them. The registry image
still provides Python, PyTorch, Lightning and the physicalai library.

This takes effect on the next deployment only; the app deployed now is
unchanged. Checked locally with the real modal 1.6.3 SDK (no deploy):
the image gets two mounts with 6 training and 20 trainer files and no
__pycache__. Untested on Modal itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
